        "TextSection": {
            "TextSectionType": "Definition",
            "Contents": "A rare fast-flow vascular anomaly located within a muscle characterized by the lesions that are usually well-defined and contain smaller vessels without or with only little obvious arteriovenous shunting on imaging. This anomaly is usually associated with pain."
        },
